>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (Digital communication and community engagement are fundamental aspects of modern social interaction, yet conventional social platforms have become increasingly fragmented, noisy, and impersonal. Users are often forced to juggle disjointed messaging tools, overwhelming public feeds, and uncurated group forums just to maintain authentic relationships and shared-interest communities. This lack of focused organization leads to digital fatigue, context switching, and communication friction for both active community creators and everyday participants.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (Beyond organizational clutter, mainstream social ecosystems face severe challenges regarding privacy, data governance, and trust. The unchecked proliferation of unverified profiles, intrusive algorithmic feeds, and insecure data handling degrades confidence in personal digital interactions. Furthermore, relying on fragmented third-party channels to exchange media, coordinate discussions, and store personal content introduces critical vulnerabilities surrounding data ownership, session security, and network scalability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (To address these systemic challenges, this project proposes the development of Bubble, a secure, fluid mobile-based community and messaging platform designed to centralize social spaces into intuitive, dedicated Bubbles. The application empowers users to seamlessly discover and engage within interest-based communities, curate personalized content feeds, and communicate in real time through secure, authenticated messaging channels. Supported by robust role-based moderation and cloud-native architecture, Bubble establishes a private, scalable, and verified ecosystem for modern digital connections)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
